no one person can make a great video  game but there are certain people in the  industry whose reputation precedes them  we spawn an infinity ward co-founder  Vincent Pella is one such individual a  man largely responsible for making one  of the most popular video games of all  time but such praise can be as much a  curse as it is a blessing when you're  trying to make something new i sat down  with Vince asked him about life after  call of duty and his four-year journey  making titanfall Vincent petticoat  founded infinity ward with jason west  and grant collie a in 2002 and went on  to reinvent first person online  multiplayer with the call of duty  franchise however in March 2010 himself  and West were dramatically fired by  Activision after allegations of contract  breaches an allegation that would  eventually be contested by the parent  court and results of Activision paying  out an undisclosed settlement in the  months that followed nearly half of the  team at infinity ward resigned a total  of forty-six many of whom were tough to  your developers and programmers who had  worked on modern warfare 2 the vast  majority of these men and women went on  to joins on pelham West at their new  studio quite appropriately named respawn  entertainment it's not the type of story  you hear very often a large group of  people leaving a successful company to  work with their former boss somewhere  else so what is it about Vincent para  and the games he makes well on the eve  of the titanfall beta launch I had the  opportunity to talk to the man and first  I asked him after years of working on  call of duty was his goal always to make  something new and once that game always  titanfall it took a while to get kind of  situated and get our flow down then we  started with different ideas you know  and there was it wasn't just like yes  we're making titanfall there was a lot  of ideas thrown out under the table we  wanted to break the boundaries when I'm  not making it completely different it's  familiar it feels like you know if you  played a footm acute ER game before you  can sit down you can grasp the controls  you know what you're doing I'd done  sequels for a while so this was more  about you know taking it to another  level doing  a little different so what is that  something new when you look at titanfall  at least on a surface level it doesn't  seem that different to other  first-person shooters it has people with  guns and buildings and customizable  Odette's player leveling it's not until  you pledge that the differences become  apparent Vince told me that the recent  beta was not only a way of stress  testing the game and getting feedback  but also a way of getting tight and fall  into people's hands so they can see what  makes it different something they've  always been keen to do you know I think  we've let people play it so there is no  you know hey I think it's gonna be good  it's I plated I touched it and I think  it's good like we know for our fans to  go out there and say that you know if I  don't know what better praise you can  get though not often is touted as other  Fame developers the name Vince Zampella  carries a lot of weight especially in  light of how Respawn Entertainment came  to be so I asked him in light of his  previous achievements how much personal  pressure did he have going into this  project I think we put a lot of pressure  on ourselves just as a team to really  make something that's the best we can  possibly do on top of that you know  there is the you want to prove like okay  you know we can do this again you know  just even for our own personal  satisfaction of you know we want to do  something good we were in games because  we love it it's just it's what we do  it's in our DNA so it's that you know it  has to be good for that reason and then  unveiling the game and having it be  received so well and it's you know it  adds another level of pressure it's like  well we have to deliver you know we've  got to deliver a multi promise it seemed  anytime I asked Vince a question about  himself he'd respond with we instead of  I as if tried to downplay his individual  importance I asked him why he and  development is a team sport you know  it's this game wouldn't exist as it is  without everybody on this team so I mean  to me it is natural it's not me I didn't  make thank you from respondent respawn  is a team of people that you know some  of us have worked together for a long  time other people are new and they've  come in and they've changed the mix and  they've been energized us and you know  so it is it's all about the team perhaps  that's the Zampella formula having a  team of people around you you can  and on a team willing to leave their  jobs or join a fledgling studio to try  and make something new and interesting  lastly just mere weeks away from the  launch of a game has been working on for  four years I asked Vince what the future  held for himself respawn I'm titanfall  it's been a long kind of road to get  where we are there's been you know a  long bumpy road to you know so to be  where we are to rally the team together  get through all the adversity that we  faced and get to a point where we're  releasing something that you know we're  proud of and as being so just it's being  accepted by the fans and by everyone you  know just so well it means a lot it's it  feels good and that wraps up the next  big game titanfall for continuing  coverage of the game including its  review once it drops in March make sure  to visit gamespot com thanks very much  for joining us all this week folks we'll  see you next time  that's a streak
 

